arez-Gavela and Kiyoshi Igusa.\n\n# GT seminar: Higher torsion of Legendrians in one-jet space\n\nDate\n    22 January 2026, 13:05–14:05\nLocation\n    Ångström Laboratory, 64119\nType\n    Seminar\nLecturer\n    Michael Sullivan (UMass Amherst)\nOrganiser\n    Matematiska Institutionen\nContact person\n    Alex Takeda\n\nMichael Sullivan (UMass Amherst) will give this seminar talk. All are welcome to join!\n\nAbstract: I'll introduce higher torsion from algebraic topology using the language of generating families for Legendrian submanifolds in standard contact one-jet spaces. I'll also propose a possible higher-dimensional generalization of rulings for such Legendrians. If the Legendrian is the lift of a nearby Lagrangian with such a ruling, then the torsion is trivial. (Although the torsion is non-trivial in general, any Legendrian which is the lift of a nearby Lagrangian and with non-trivial torsion would disprove the Nearby Lagrangian Conjecture.) This is joint work in progress with Dani Alvarez-Gavela and Kiyoshi Igusa.\n\nThis is a talk in our Geometry and Topology Seminar Series.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAMS :: Notices of the American Mathematical Society (https://doi.org/10.1090/NOTI2238)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.6 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Ball packingsWe next try to pack a symplectic manifold by balls as densely as possible.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLegendrian and Lagrangian higher torsion — Plain-Language Explanation | Gist.Science (https://gist.science/paper/2603.28007)\nciteturn1search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Crawled: last week; This paper introduces Legendrian higher torsion, a new family of invariants for Legendrians in $J^1M$J 1 M derived from higher Reidemeister torsion of associated fibre bundles, and demonstrates that while the tube torsion of nearby Lagrangians relates to the Pontryag